  "term": "OCD",
  "definition": "OCD is a mental disorder in which a person has persistent, recurring irrational thoughts called obsessions that cause marked anxiety. The person then engages in repetitive, excessive behaviors, called compulsions, in an attempt to reduce that anxiety.",
